      "content": "That's a very strong position to take. So, if we follow that logic, are you saying that any legislation passed for the purpose of modern digital security is essentially illegitimate because it breaks that Lockean foundation? It sounds like you're saying the state has no moral authority to implement these tools, even if they are technically effective at preventing harm. Is there any version of the social contract that could actually accommodate these modern realities, or is the concept itself essentially dead in the age of the internet?",
